- Story & Context: Marja stood on the roof of the relay station clutching a rusted iron rod, her hair standing on end as the first bolt tore the cloud cover open. The air tasted like scorched copper, and she felt the static burn through her boots before the signal locked in. She didn't scream; she began to chant the forbidden sequence into the wind. "The clouds are teeth that swallow the light," she sang, her voice trembling in perfect sync with the flickering transmitter lamp.
